    "U": "证据片段：'These in clude' 和 'functional re quirements' 包含拼写错误（例如 'in clude' 应为 'include'），降低文本可读性，影响理解。",
    "A": "证据片段：'the manner in wh ich the soft ware will be designed, developed, and dep loyed' 中 'manner' 一词模糊，可能导致对非功能需求范围的不同解释，产生歧义。",
    "C": "证据片段：整句 'These in clude the functional re quirements, ... and the plan fo r implementation of Pontis 5.0.' 作为需求条目，没有指定具体可操作需求，可能不正确或不完整。",
    "V": "证据片段：需求中没有提及验证方法或标准，如测试用例或验收条件，使其无法测试或验证。"
  },
  "suggestions": {
    "U": "纠正所有拼写错误，例如：'These include the functional requirements, which describe the operations that users must perform using Pontis 5.0, the non-functional requirements, which describe the manner in which the software will be designed, developed, and deployed, and the plan for implementation of Pontis 5.0.'",
    "A": "将模糊描述具体化，例如：'Non-functional requirements shall specify constraints on software design, development, and deployment, such as performance metrics (e.g., response time < 2 seconds) and security standards.'",
    "C": "如果意图是定义需求结构，改写为：'The requirements documentation for Pontis 5.0 shall include: (a) functional requirements specifying user operations, (b) non-functional requirements specifying design and deployment constraints, and (c) an implementation plan.' 否则，指定原子需求。",
    "V": "添加可验证元素，例如：'Each requirement must be verifiable through defined acceptance criteria, such as user tests for functional requirements and benchmark tests for non-functional requirements.'"
  },
  "issues": [
    {
      "type": "U",
      "evidence": "'These in clude' 和 'functional re quirements'",
      "rewrite": "纠正为 'These include' 和 'functional requirements'"
    },
    {
      "type": "A",
      "evidence": "'the manner in wh ich the soft ware will be designed, developed, and dep loyed'",
      "rewrite": "替换为 'specific constraints on software design, development, and deployment, e.g., performance requirement: system uptime of 99.9%'"
    },
    {
      "type": "C",
      "evidence": "整句没有具体需求内容",
      "rewrite": "改写为原子需求，例如 'Functional requirement: Users shall be able to log in to Pontis 5.0 using a username and password.'"
    },
    {
      "type": "V",
      "evidence": "没有验证标准",
      "rewrite": "添加验证方法，例如 'All requirements shall be accompanied by test cases; for example, for a login function, test case: verify successful login with valid credentials.'"
    }
  ]
}

