  "rationales": {"U":"原文存在多处拼写错误（如'in clude'、're quirements'、'tha t'、'per form'、'des cribe'、'wh ich'、'fo r'）和空格断裂，严重阻碍可读性；'the manner in which the software will be designed, developed, and deployed'语义宽泛、无具体约束，用户无法形成一致理解；证据片段：'These in clude the functional re quirements, which describe the operations tha t user s must per form using Pontis 5.0'","A":"'operations that users must perform'未定义操作主体（哪类用户？）、触发条件（何时执行？）、输入/输出（执行什么？产出什么？），且'manner in which the software will be designed, developed, and deployed'属于过程管理范畴而非软件需求，违反需求应描述系统行为而非开发活动的原则；证据片段：'the non-functional requirements, which describe the manner in which the software will be designed, developed, and deployed'","C":"该条将实施计划（implementation plan）与功能/非功能需求并列，混淆需求类型边界；标准需求分类中，实施计划不属于需求条目，属项目管理内容，因此分类逻辑错误；证据片段：'and the plan for implementation of Pontis 5.0'","V":"全文无任何可测试的判定准则——未指定功能需支持的具体操作名称、参数、前置/后置条件；未定义非功能要求的度量指标（如性能响应时间、可用性百分比、部署环境配置）；'plan for implementation'完全不可验证；证据片段：'the plan for implementation of Pontis 5.0'"},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Replace with: 'This document contains three categories of requirements for Pontis 5.0: (1) functional requirements, specifying observable system behaviors triggered by users; (2) non-functional requirements, specifying measurable quality attributes such as response time, availability, and security; and (3) project constraints and implementation assumptions, documented separately in Appendix A.'","A":"Replace with: 'Functional requirements shall specify user-initiated actions, their valid inputs, expected system responses, and success/failure conditions. Non-functional requirements shall specify quantifiable targets (e.g., \"95% of UI interactions respond within 2 seconds\") and testable acceptance criteria.'","C":"Replace with: 'This specification defines only functional and non-functional requirements for Pontis 5.0. Implementation planning, scheduling, and resource allocation are outside the scope of this requirements document and governed by the Project Management Plan (PMP-2024).'", "V":"Replace with: 'Each functional requirement shall be uniquely identified (e.g., FR-001), include a traceable use case or user story, and define at least one pass/fail verification method (e.g., test procedure, inspection, demonstration). Each non-functional requirement shall specify a measurable attribute, target value, unit, and measurement method (e.g., \"System shall authenticate users within 1.5 s (±0.1 s) under 100 concurrent sessions, measured via JMeter load test\").'"}, 
